-- title:
--   Toric m-torsion via A-sections with trivial abelian-quotient reduction
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ is a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data for $p, M, H$ at $A$: a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` with `barPt A` followed by $\sigma_A$ equal to `genPt p`, a scheme $X$ with structure morphism $f$ to `base p`, a relative group law $\Lambda.L$ on $f$, and parametrisations of the sections of $f$ over `genPt p` and over `resPt A ≫ σA`. Let $O$ be a Néron object at $p$ for these data, with structure morphism $O.g \colon G \to$ `base p` and parametrisation `O.pts` of the sections of $O.g$ over `genPt p` by $J_H(M) = \operatorname{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $m > 0$ be coprime to $p$ and let $x \in J_H(M)$ be killed by $m$. Then $x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m\,\chi$ attached to the $A$-algebra maps $\chi$ from `muCoord A O.toricRank m` to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, if and only if there is a section $s \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to G$ with $s$ followed by $O.g$ equal to $\sigma_A$, such that the morphism underlying $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ is `barPt A` followed by $s$, and such that for both $i \in \{0,1\}$ the image of the restriction of $s$ along `resPt A` under the special-fibre morphism $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$, taken via `fibreMap`, is the identity section $\Lambda.L.\mathrm{one}$ over `resPt A ≫ σA`.
--
--   This identifies the toric part of the $m$-torsion, for $m$ prime to $p$, with those points whose (necessarily unique) extension to an $A$-valued section of the Néron object reduces into the torus, the latter condition being expressed by the vanishing of the two abelian-quotient coordinates on the special fibre. It is the level-$\Gamma_H(M)$ form of the criterion used to control the action of inertia at $p$, and is invoked in the results that place $\sigma \cdot x - x$ in the toric subgroup for $\sigma$ in the inertia group.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JHNeronObjectAtP_mem_toricPts_iff_exists_fibreMap_abqFibre_eq_one.lean

